Description: Speech Dispatcher module: text normalization and stress marks
 When liblinux-tts-text (package linux-tts-text, from linux-tts) is
 installed, the module passes the text through it before RHVoice reads it:
 numbers, dates, units and abbreviations become words (rn for Russian,
 zyphra-textnorm for other languages), and Russian gets ё from the stress
 dictionaries, with "+" stress marks when languages.Russian.stress_marker=+
 is set in RHVoice.conf. Only the text between the SSML tags changes. The
 language is that of the first voice of the profile. Keys TextNormalization,
 TextStress... in the module's configuration file; without the library the
 text is read as before.
